WEBVTT

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.650
Starting tomorrow, I'm going 
to China for high-altitude training.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:17.490
I wanted to encourage
Kiyose before leaving Japan,

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:20.910
<b>Famous Confections</b>

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.340
but I'm still not familiar
with your home base.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.500
Thanks for the escort.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.370
Home base?

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.810
They've got an exchange student?

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:32.200
I know. I wish they'd run
an all-Japanese team.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.070
The school's probably paying
for it to promote themselves.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.810
They're the words of amateurs.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.520
Don't let them distract you.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.980
I know how you feel.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.090
People have always dealt with that criticism.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.000
There are two reasons 
not to let it bother you.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:55.240
First, there's the logic that recruiting
an exchange student is unfair.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.950
What about the Olympics then?

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.300
It's only natural that there's some
difference in individual physical ability.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.320
Moreover, sports are fair and impartial.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.220
Those who question its
fairness don't understand

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.250
what it means to compete 
in the same sport on the same stage.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.140
The other reason is that they
think winning is everything.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:24.890
<b>Mens Relay — “Spectacular Achievement”</b>

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.890
Is the only thing that matters that
a Japanese person places first?

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:28.850
<b>New Japanese Record</b>

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:28.850
<b>Spectacular Achieve in Track and Field</b>

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.850
No. That's not the true
nature of competition.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:31.570
<b>Mens
10000m
Finals

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.570
Even if I finish first,

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:35.290
if I feel like I've lost to myself,
then it's a loss.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.580
In this world where times and
standings change at dizzying speeds,

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.990
what determines who's the best?

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.840
Don't we keep running because there are
ideals and goals we value more than that?

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.810
You've gathered good members.
It's his kind of team.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.260
Are you and Haiji close?

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.370
We were teammates in high school.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:12.100
He was supposed to be wearing
a Rikudo uniform, too.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:12.820
What?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:37.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.960
<b>— 4 Years Earlier —</b>

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.920
<b>Congratulations Track and Field Team</b>

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.920
One, two, three, four.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.510
Five, six, seven, eight.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.140
Two, two, three, four.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.710
Five, six, seven, eight.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.130
Three, two, three, four.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:14.660
Five, six, seven, eight.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.270
Four, two, three, four—

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.730
Those fireflies you hate
so much will be back soon.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.990
I don't hate them.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.700
There are just too many around here.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:29.010
This is our last year. Savor it.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.160
Let's go together.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.530
To Rikudo. Then we can—

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.380
It's already been decided.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.630
But you were recruited.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.930
The care they offer 
their athletes is top-class.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.050
I've already spent two years with this leg.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:51.360
I know my body better than anyone else.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.560
What did the coach say?

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.560
“Be patient.” That's all.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.910
That was a lot of talking for him.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.910
I'm happy about this year, though.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.350
Last year, I didn't get to run 
with you once because of PT.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.330
My athletic career may be over, but we—

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.450
It's not over!

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.600
Believe in yourself.

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.670
I'm not that strong.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.760
He should be telling you this himself.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:39.400
If he hasn't told you yet, then he probably
doesn't think it's the right time.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.090
I shouldn't have said anything.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.860
<b><i>And Then, Morning</i></b>

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:55.720
Haiji isn't back yet.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.230
He's not answering his phone either.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.430
I see.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.950
I'm sorry.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:04.780
Then, the next time I'll see
him will be in the new year.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:08.180
Good luck to both of us.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.190
Tell him that.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.100
I will.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.420
Oh, this is for you guys.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.690
Red bean paste. Better than cream, right?

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:19.320
Oh, yeah. Thank you.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.570
I'll be waiting at Hakone!

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:30.260
I wish I could've seen him.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.910
What did you talk about with Fujioka?

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.620
What did we...

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.850
I was just wondering if you got along.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:40.090
More or less. It went fine.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.080
What does that mean?

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:43.840
Haiji.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.800
I think I'm finally starting to understand.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:51.030
I mean, I don't understand yet.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.300
What are you talking about?

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.570
What it means to be strong.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:07:00.140
You told me about how Fujioka is strong.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.310
I understand now what you meant.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:08.650
He's been pursuing a much higher
level of running than I've been.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.150
It's hard to explain, but—

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.990
You can, too.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.860
Become strong, Kakeru.

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:24.870
I will.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:29.980
By the way, I brought Fujioka here once,

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.550
but he didn't last ten seconds.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.510
<b>Tsuru-no-yu</b>

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.320
In that regard, I'm stronger than him.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.000
You two sure are close.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.480
<b>Race Completion Certificates Issued Here
</b>Saitama Ageo Athletic Field

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.440
<b>Welcome to Ageo</b>

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:48.150
<b>Welcome to Ageo!
Ageo City Marathon/Ageo City Half Marathon
Sponsors: City of Ageo/Ageo Board of Education/
Ageo Sports Association/Saitama Track and Field Association</b>

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:46.080
The Ageo City Marathon is about
as long as Hakone's sections.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.150
It's the perfect dry run.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:51.680
Make sure you experience 
what it's like to run on city streets

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.210
and the tension of a race.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:58.160
Anyway, I won't say anything else.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.750
Go enjoy yourselves.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.710
No one's enjoying himself more than you.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:04.920
Haiji!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.840
They said they want to do 
“the mountains of Hakone.”

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:09.770
What?

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.800
What are you talking about, Hana?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:16.010
Didn't you say hearing
Haiji do that fires you up?

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.370
Hana's such a good girl.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:19.470
Yeah.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:23.730
The twins missed their
opportunity to apologize to Haiji.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:27.160
And she's giving them 
a chance to return to normal.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:30.110
Now we wait for Haiji to come through.

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.660
You want to do it?

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:35.740
You guys want to do it that badly?

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.660
Kiyose Haiji doesn't play along that easily.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.290
Come on. Put out your hands.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:44.040
Hey!

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.500
Are you okay?

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.950
Your face is bright red.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:48.960
Don't worry about it!

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.920
Go ahead!

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.380
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:54.840
The steepest in?

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.090
In the world, right?

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.680
It's in the world.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.510
In the world.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.650
Perfect! You can do it!

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:07.650
Should we not have joined them?

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:10.110
You're pretty bad, too.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.140
What?

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:37.380
<b>Ageo City Marathon</b>

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.490
<b>Sendai J High School Track Coach
Claims incident with KK is “in the past...” 
and refuses to speak...</b>

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.490
<b>Reveals Actual Name</b>

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:04.850
Sendai J High School track
coach claims incident with KK

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:09.040
is “in the past” and refuses to speak?

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.630
If you weren't going to talk,
don't accept an interview request!

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:15.790
J and KK? They're identifying them!

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.340
Don't let it bother you.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.680
<b>Chairman's Office</b>

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.390
For this incident...

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:27.810
We're terribly sorry!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:28.770
<b>Incoming Call
Home</b>

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:30.480
It's me.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:34.280
Are you okay? I read the magazine article.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:38.700
Dad's mad, okay? 
Are you sure you're okay?

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:42.440
People in the country like to talk.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:45.260
Put yourself in our shoes. Please.

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:46.820
I know.

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:49.110
What are you doing for New Year's?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.200
I'm not going home.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:53.310
Don't tell me you've made bad friends in—

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:54.670
I'm running at Hakone!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:03.430
Sorry. I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:06.680
I don't get along with my parents.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:12.440
I forgot to tell you before,
but neither do I.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.520
We haven't met once since I started college.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:17.230
It's not serious.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:22.020
My mom got remarried. She's living
with a man I don't know very well.

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:23.950
I don't know how close we're supposed to be.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.500
Oh.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:29.670
I don't like close relationships,
parents or otherwise.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.670
Everyone's alone.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:34.630
It's stupid to try to understand others.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:41.550
But living here's been 
throwing me off my pace.

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:49.220
The track team's short distance team
offered to be our water station staff.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.800
It's a first for all of us,

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:53.940
so I'm thinking we should 
make time next week to rehearse.

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:57.400
I agree. What about the
shopping center vendors?

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.350
I'm having them arrange transportation
and lodging for the athletes,

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.360
as well as recording our times.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:06.560
Also, about the forms we're submitting
to the student association...

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:09.830
What would we do without Shindo?

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.090
He never accepts my offers for help.

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:14.540
Have you been getting enough sleep?

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:18.000
I'm great. This is actually fine for me.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.980
At least there wasn't a huge
commotion over the article.

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:25.430
We have our landlord 
to thank for handling it quickly.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:28.430
The school has agreed to wait and see, too.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.140
That guy actually does his job, huh?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:35.350
He bragged about being
called Tazaki the Beggar.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.350
Is that something to brag about?

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:38.560
Thanks for waiting.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:40.280
I bought liquor.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.020
Yeah!

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:44.490
Let's gather in the twins' room.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.060
<b>Merry Christmas</b>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:28.870
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.750
<b>January
January 1st
Tuesday
New Year's Day
New Year's Day is the day for planning
It's tomorrow!!!
Yeah!!! I'm so nervous heh heh
We'll be popular tomorrow!!</b>

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.900
<b>Hakone</b>

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:53.120
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:15.760
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.660
You'll tire yourself out
if you move too much.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:22.730
I'll now tell all of you who
I've signed up for each section.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:33.160
First, section one. Prince.

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.280
What?

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.560
Are you trying to throw the race?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:40.100
I can't imagine anyone else
running section one.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.160
You're the only one who can
stand there so calmly

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:45.840
that you seem almost oblivious,
even with all that attention on you.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.870
Is that a compliment?

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:50.050
Naturally, I'm not throwing the race.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.510
I made this line-up to win.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:53.910
Are you sure?

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:57.470
There have been a lot of fast-paced
developments the past few years.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:16:01.690
It's possible this year will be
slow-paced in response to that.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:07.620
Even if Prince falls behind,
we'll get it back in section two.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.500
Musa, that's your job.

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.420
Seriously?

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.410
You can do it, Musa.

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:24.620
H-Hold on! Kakeru should run that section.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.700
Right, Kakeru? Right?

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:28.110
You heard him.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:33.480
You can run ten kilometers
in about twenty-nine minutes.

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:35.800
That's on par with other runners.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:38.210
But more than that,

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:41.720
you've been the most considerate and
encouraging towards the rest of the team.

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:44.270
I can't imagine anyone but you running it.

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:46.650
That was my thinking, too.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:50.730
Oh, no!

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:54.340
Section three, Jota.

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:56.870
Section four, Joji

00:16:56.870 --> 00:17:00.870
Isn't section three by the sea?
I love that course.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.580
I'll buy you guys some
fish cakes from Ogawara.

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:07.960
Their sections sound way more fun.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.090
Accept your fate, Musa.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:12.130
Section five, Shindo.

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:14.550
No objections.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:17.630
Section six, Yuki.

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:18.720
Hey, wait!

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:21.470
I'm section six? That's ridiculous.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:25.050
I've watched how all of you run
for the past ten months.

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:28.650
Your core strength and stable
center of gravity are the best, Yuki.

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:32.490
You're the only one 
who can ride down Hakone.

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:34.980
I'm setting you up.

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:36.930
Want something to drink?

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:39.990
Section seven, Nico-chan Senpai.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.700
Section eight, King.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.890
Just like I expected.

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:46.410
You were wrong at Musa.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.370
At this point, the runners
will start to scatter.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:51.380
You might be running alone.

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:55.590
The race for seeds will become intense
during these two important sections.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:59.370
I know you'll be able to stay
calm and maintain your pace.

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:02.530
You're trying to earn a seeded spot?

00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:06.200
Of course. That's why those
sections are important.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:09.770
The return half's section two,
section nine, Kakeru.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:16.820
I don't see Fujioka.

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:22.630
By last-minute registration, if Rikudo's
Fujioka isn't signed up for the first half,

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.860
we'll know Rikudo's strategy
is to wait out the first half

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:28.710
and attack during the second.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:30.670
Which means...

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:32.880
Bring it on.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:36.930
Finally, section ten.

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:39.170
I'll take responsibility
by finishing the race.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:42.900
Jota, Joji.

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:46.640
I'll show you the top.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:50.580
No, we'll experience it together.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:51.720
All of us.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:56.070
<b>Hakone</b>

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:59.490
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:03.110
Happy New Year.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:07.080
<b>January 2nd</b>

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:06.210
The new year arrived quietly this year.

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:11.040
Runners, get ready to move!

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:17.990
Coaches, please come to the admin vehicle!

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:19.650
Now I can die in peace.

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:22.380
I'll be watching from my box seat.

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:26.390
<b>Hakone Ekiden</b>

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:32.350
